        "Content": "No. 18 The Oaks enjoys a convenient position within Oakwood Lawns, an established residential development located close to the centre of Edenderry, Co. Offaly. The property benefits from a quiet residential setting while remaining within easy reach of the town`s excellent range of shops, schools, sporting facilities and everyday amenities. Edenderry is one of the principal towns in the east Offaly area and provides an extensive selection of services including supermarkets, independent retailers, cafés, restaurants, pharmacies, banks and professional services. The town is well catered for by major supermarkets including Tesco, Dunnes Stores, Lidl and Aldi, together with a variety of local shops and businesses.\r\n\r\nFamilies are particularly well served, with a good selection of primary and secondary schools available in Edenderry and the surrounding area, together with numerous childcare facilities. The town also offers a strong choice of sporting and recreational amenities, including Edenderry GAA Club, Edenderry Rugby Club, Edenderry Golf Club, soccer clubs, gyms and other community facilities. One of Edenderry`s notable recreational amenities is the Grand Canal, which runs through the town and provides attractive waterside walks and routes for walking, running and cycling. There are also numerous countryside walks and outdoor amenities throughout the surrounding north Kildare and Offaly countryside. The location is particularly convenient for those commuting throughout the Greater Dublin Area and Midlands. Edenderry has good road connections to Enfield, Kinnegad, Maynooth, Naas, Newbridge and Dublin, with access to the M4 motorway at Enfield providing a direct route towards Dublin and the M50. The M6 and wider national motorway network are also readily accessible via the surrounding road\r\nnetwork.\r\n\r\nPublic transport connections are available from Edenderry, with regular bus services connecting the town with Dublin and surrounding towns, making the location a practical option for commuters who wish to enjoy a more relaxed residential setting while retaining accessibility to the capital. The neighbouring towns of Enfield, Kinnegad and Clane, together with the larger centres of Maynooth, Newbridge and Naas, are also within comfortable driving distance and provide additional shopping, employment, educational and recreational amenities. Overall, No. 18 The Oaks offers an attractive combination of an established residential setting, excellent local amenities, schools and sporting facilities, together with convenient transport connections to Dublin, Kildare and the wider Midlands\r\n\r\nNo. 18 The Oaks is a superb four-bedroom detached family home extending to approximately 140 sq.m. (1,507 sq.ft.), completed in 2025 and presented to the market in exceptional, show-home condition. Beautifully finished and tastefully upgraded throughout, the property offers bright, generously proportioned accommodation complemented by a particularly impressive, low-maintenance rear garden. To the front, the property is approached over a large cobblelock driveway, providing ample off-street parking and enhanced by smart Portuguese laurel planting.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are immediately struck by the quality of the finish. The welcoming entrance hall features large-format flagstone-style floor tiles and attractive wall panelling, creating a stylish introduction to the home. Off the hallway is a cosy yet spacious dual-aspect living room, centred around an impressive custom-built media wall incorporating an electric fire, recessed TV area and integrated LED lighting. A feature bay window adds further character while allowing excellent natural light into the room. The kitchen/dining room forms the heart of the home and has been finished to an excellent standard. The bespoke fitted kitchen incorporates a central island together with a distinctive vintage-style glass splashback, providing an attractive focal point to the room. French doors and an additional side window allow natural light to flood the space while providing a seamless connection with the rear garden. A useful store room, separate utility room and guest W.C. complete the ground-floor accommodation. Upstairs, a bright and spacious landing provides access to four well-proportioned bedrooms, together with a useful storage press. The principal bedroom benefits from its own en-suite, while the remaining three bedrooms are served by a stylish family bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe rear garden is undoubtedly another standout feature of No. 18. Designed to provide an attractive yet virtually maintenance-free outdoor space, the garden has been extensively landscaped with beautiful sandstone-style paving incorporating decorative cobble-sett detailing, complemented by an artificial lawn. The generous patio provides an exceptional outdoor entertaining area with ample space for dining, lounging and BBQ facilities. It is an ideal setting for entertaining family and friends, hosting summer BBQs or simply relaxing outdoors, effectively creating an extension of the living accommodation during the warmer months. Completed only in 2025, No. 18 combines the comfort, energy efficiency and low maintenance of a nearly new home with a level of finish, upgrading and landscaping rarely found in a standard new-build property. The result is an impressive turnkey family home extending to c. 140 sq.m., where considerable thought and attention have already gone into both the internal accommodation and outdoor spaces"
      }
